{"title":"Max flow, one augmenting path at a time","sub":"Find an s→t path with spare capacity, push as much as it allows, repeat. Edge labels are flow / capacity.","kind":"graph","interval":1500,"scenarioLabel":"Example","legend":[["b","augmenting path"],["a","used backwards: flow cancelled"],["c","carrying flow"],["good","saturated"],["bad","the minimum cut"]],"scenarios":[{"name":"Edmonds-Karp","frames":[{"caption":"Push as much as possible from s to t. Edge labels are <b>flow / capacity</b>. Edmonds-Karp repeatedly finds the shortest path with spare room, and fills it.","nodes":{},"edges":{},"edgeLabels":{"s-v1":"0/16","s-v2":"0/13","v1-v3":"0/12","v2-v1":"0/4","v2-v4":"0/14","v3-v2":"0/9","v3-t":"0/20","v4-v3":"0/7","v4-t":"0/4"},"stats":[["Flow from s",0]]},{"caption":"Augmenting path <b>s→v1→v3→t</b>, with room for 12.","nodes":{},"edges":{"s-v1":"b","v1-v3":"b","v3-t":"b"},"edgeLabels":{"s-v1":"0/16","s-v2":"0/13","v1-v3":"0/12","v2-v1":"0/4","v2-v4":"0/14","v3-v2":"0/9","v3-t":"0/20","v4-v3":"0/7","v4-t":"0/4"},"stats":[["Flow from s",0]]},{"caption":"Push 12 along it. Saturated edges turn green.","nodes":{},"edges":{"s-v1":"c","v1-v3":"good","v3-t":"c"},"edgeLabels":{"s-v1":"12/16","s-v2":"0/13","v1-v3":"12/12","v2-v1":"0/4","v2-v4":"0/14","v3-v2":"0/9","v3-t":"12/20","v4-v3":"0/7","v4-t":"0/4"},"stats":[["Flow from s",12]]},{"caption":"Augmenting path <b>s→v2→v4→t</b>, with room for 4.","nodes":{},"edges":{"s-v1":"c","v1-v3":"good","v3-t":"c","s-v2":"b","v2-v4":"b","v4-t":"b"},"edgeLabels":{"s-v1":"12/16","s-v2":"0/13","v1-v3":"12/12","v2-v1":"0/4","v2-v4":"0/14","v3-v2":"0/9","v3-t":"12/20","v4-v3":"0/7","v4-t":"0/4"},"stats":[["Flow from s",12]]},{"caption":"Push 4 along it. Saturated edges turn green.","nodes":{},"edges":{"s-v1":"c","s-v2":"c","v1-v3":"good","v2-v4":"c","v3-t":"c","v4-t":"good"},"edgeLabels":{"s-v1":"12/16","s-v2":"4/13","v1-v3":"12/12","v2-v1":"0/4","v2-v4":"4/14","v3-v2":"0/9","v3-t":"12/20","v4-v3":"0/7","v4-t":"4/4"},"stats":[["Flow from s",16]]},{"caption":"Augmenting path <b>s→v2→v4→v3→t</b>, with room for 7.","nodes":{},"edges":{"s-v1":"c","s-v2":"b","v1-v3":"good","v2-v4":"b","v3-t":"b","v4-t":"good","v4-v3":"b"},"edgeLabels":{"s-v1":"12/16","s-v2":"4/13","v1-v3":"12/12","v2-v1":"0/4","v2-v4":"4/14","v3-v2":"0/9","v3-t":"12/20","v4-v3":"0/7","v4-t":"4/4"},"stats":[["Flow from s",16]]},{"caption":"Push 7 along it. Saturated edges turn green.","nodes":{},"edges":{"s-v1":"c","s-v2":"c","v1-v3":"good","v2-v4":"c","v3-t":"c","v4-v3":"good","v4-t":"good"},"edgeLabels":{"s-v1":"12/16","s-v2":"11/13","v1-v3":"12/12","v2-v1":"0/4","v2-v4":"11/14","v3-v2":"0/9","v3-t":"19/20","v4-v3":"7/7","v4-t":"4/4"},"stats":[["Flow from s",23]]},{"caption":"No path with spare room is left, so the flow is maximal: <b>23</b>. The vertices s can still reach (blue) form one side of a cut; its crossing edges (red) have capacity 12 + 7 + 4 = <b>23</b>. Max flow equals min cut.","nodes":{"v1":{"cls":"a"},"s":{"cls":"a"},"v2":{"cls":"a"},"v4":{"cls":"a"}},"edges":{"s-v1":"c","s-v2":"c","v1-v3":"bad","v2-v4":"c","v3-t":"c","v4-v3":"bad","v4-t":"bad"},"edgeLabels":{"s-v1":"12/16","s-v2":"11/13","v1-v3":"12/12","v2-v1":"0/4","v2-v4":"11/14","v3-v2":"0/9","v3-t":"19/20","v4-v3":"7/7","v4-t":"4/4"},"stats":[["Flow from s",23]]}],"graph":{"w":580,"h":320,"r":21,"nodes":[{"id":"s","x":50,"y":160},{"id":"v1","x":200,"y":60},{"id":"v2","x":200,"y":260},{"id":"v3","x":380,"y":60},{"id":"v4","x":380,"y":260},{"id":"t","x":530,"y":160}],"edges":[{"u":"s","v":"v1","w":"0/16","dir":true},{"u":"s","v":"v2","w":"0/13","dir":true},{"u":"v1","v":"v3","w":"0/12","dir":true},{"u":"v2","v":"v1","w":"0/4","dir":true},{"u":"v2","v":"v4","w":"0/14","dir":true},{"u":"v3","v":"v2","w":"0/9","dir":true},{"u":"v3","v":"t","w":"0/20","dir":true},{"u":"v4","v":"v3","w":"0/7","dir":true},{"u":"v4","v":"t","w":"0/4","dir":true}]}},{"name":"Why backward edges matter","frames":[{"caption":"Every edge holds 1. The best answer is obvious: s→a→t and s→b→t, for a flow of 2. But suppose the first path found is unlucky.","edges":{},"edgeLabels":{"s-a":"0/1","s-b":"0/1","a-b":"0/1","a-t":"0/1","b-t":"0/1"},"stats":[["Flow from s",0]]},{"caption":"First path: <b>s→a→b→t</b>, through the middle edge.","edges":{"s-a":"b","a-b":"b","b-t":"b"},"edgeLabels":{"s-a":"0/1","s-b":"0/1","a-b":"0/1","a-t":"0/1","b-t":"0/1"},"stats":[["Flow from s",0]]},{"caption":"Push 1. Now a→t and s→b look useless: there's no forward route left from s to t. Without backward edges, we'd be stuck at 1.","edges":{"s-a":"good","a-b":"good","b-t":"good"},"edgeLabels":{"s-a":"1/1","s-b":"0/1","a-b":"1/1","a-t":"0/1","b-t":"1/1"},"stats":[["Flow from s",1]]},{"caption":"But the residual graph has a backward edge b→a, worth the 1 unit on a→b. Path <b>s→b→a→t</b> uses it.","edges":{"s-a":"good","a-b":"a","b-t":"good","s-b":"b","a-t":"b"},"edgeLabels":{"s-a":"1/1","s-b":"0/1","a-b":"1/1","a-t":"0/1","b-t":"1/1"},"stats":[["Flow from s",1]]},{"caption":"Push 1. Going backwards across a→b <b>cancels</b> the earlier flow there: the unit that went a→b→t is rerouted to a→t, and the new unit takes b→t. Flow 2: optimal.","edges":{"s-a":"good","s-b":"good","a-t":"good","b-t":"good"},"edgeLabels":{"s-a":"1/1","s-b":"1/1","a-b":"0/1","a-t":"1/1","b-t":"1/1"},"stats":[["Flow from s",2]]}],"interval":1700,"graph":{"w":580,"h":320,"r":21,"nodes":[{"id":"s","x":60,"y":160},{"id":"a","x":290,"y":50},{"id":"b","x":290,"y":270},{"id":"t","x":520,"y":160}],"edges":[{"u":"s","v":"a","w":"0/1","dir":true},{"u":"s","v":"b","w":"0/1","dir":true},{"u":"a","v":"b","w":"0/1","dir":true},{"u":"a","v":"t","w":"0/1","dir":true},{"u":"b","v":"t","w":"0/1","dir":true}]}}]}